app,action_file,verdict,evidence,fix
app,動作檔,判定,證據,修正
P0,P0-appstorage.actions,missed,"Reads ""Launch count ...: 5"" and the status line is the onAppear text ""Window appeared. Incremented @AppStorage to 5."" No click changed it. On GTK the buttons span frame y 160-193, so all four clicks at y 197 fell just below them.","origin=frame: Increment (220,176), Reset (358,176)"
P1,P1-dialogs-and-sheets.actions,missed,"""Open: No open result yet"". Folder and Save read Cancelled (those clicks landed). Open file dialog spans frame y 169-203, so the click at y 207 is 4pt below it. Open root sheet spans y 313-347, so the click at y 309 is 4pt above it (no sheet evidence).","origin=frame: Open file dialog (310,186), Open root sheet (310,330). Folder (310,241) and Save (310,275) are fine"
P2,P2-controls-and-visual-states.actions,missed,"""options: 5"" and ""Always enabled (1)"", but Length is 96 (expected 3). Set 12345/Clear at y 243 are above their buttons (y 251-283). The TextEditor click at (400,285) hit empty space. Enable button row at y 446 is above its button (y 482-515), so the row stays disabled. Always enabled (1) came from the Cancel click at (199,528), which landed on it. The Delete row and Allow window resizing were not hit.","origin=frame: Set 12345 (69,267), Clear (161,267), TextEditor (300,370), Enable button row (93,499), Disabled action (77,541), Always enabled (235,541), Disabled toggle (387,541), second Delete (142,607), Cancel (228,607), Allow window resizing (105,680)"
P3,P3-sidebar-detail-and-image-size.actions,effect,"Detail C highlighted, ""Image size: Medium, scale: 1.6x"", ""Selected detail: C""",
P4,P4-rows-callbacks-and-scrolling.actions,missed,"Partial: the final claim holds (""Rows: 275, rows 200-249, update tick: 3"", selected row 249 from Run last). But ""callbacks: 2"" where 3 was expected: Run 0 (60,344) fell in the gap between ""Load next rows"" and the first Run row, and ""Run 5"" (60,514) hit the 4th row (Run 3)","Run 0 at 60,370; Run 5 at 60,611 (frame; rows step about 48pt from y370)"
P5,P5-two-windows-and-stacked-alerts.actions,defect,"A+B+C button landed and all three alerts were dismissed, but p5-debug-events.log lists Alert A, then B, then C dismissed: on GTK the earliest alert is on top/queued (expected C, B, A). Separately, ""Open another window"" (270,202) lands just below the button (alerts logged as ""Main:"", not ""Secondary:""), so the two-window half was not exercised.","also re-aim Open another window to 295,181 frame"
P7,P7-two-lists-and-a-split-view.actions,effect,"End state matches the last three buttons: Selection: Cherry (plain list highlights Cherry), split list cleared (""No sidebar selection""), and the ""A longer message..."" text is shown. Intermediate row clicks cannot be checked; on GTK they fall about one row off (e.g. the 50,252 ""Apple"" click is on Banana).",
P8,P8-nested-scroll-views.actions,defect,"moves land on the intended views (red box, outer rows, H strip, by window layout), all six wheel events posted (log -scroll via HID), but nothing moved: outer view still starts at Outer row 0 after the final dy 3 on the strip, H strip at H0; same as P72 where scrolls stays 0 -- synthesised wheel events appear not to reach GtkBackend scroll views/handlers on macOS (could be the harness's HID path rather than the backend; no GTK scroll has been seen to work in this slice)",
P9,P9-field-height-and-clipped-text.actions,defect,"typing, Force update and width buttons landed (field hi, secure shows 3 dots, updates: 2, width 0 px), but at zero width GTK lays the line out one hyphenated character per line in a tall column at the left edge, spilling far past the 0-width frame and pushing the buttons down ~120 pt; no blue band visible -- the 'nothing may spill' check fails",
P10,P10-overlays-and-hit-testing.actions,effect,"Direct clicks 2, Covered clicks 2, Hidden clicks 2. The overlay toggle is off, so it was removed.",
P10,P10-taplabel.actions,effect,"Direct clicks 1, Covered clicks 1, Hidden clicks 1.",
P11,P11-sliders-scrollbar-and-picker.actions,missed,"Collide landed (minimum 50 / maximum 50, ""Both at 50""), but ""writes: min 0, max 0"" means the drag after Reset wrote nothing: y 276 falls between the two sliders (y 250 and 290). The date still reads Oct 16, 2026 (launch day, expected one month later). GTK's compact DatePicker has no month stepper; the clicks at (263,534/544) land on the ""Compact DatePicker sizing"" label row.","origin=frame: drag the min knob from about (42,250) along y 250; the max slider is at y 290. Date: open the date dropdown at (170,566) and use the calendar's month arrow (needs GTK measuring). Reference button is at (594,566)"
P12,P12-tabs-margins-and-toggles.actions,missed,"""Selected tab: Second, counter: 2"", but Second is the launch tab. The tab clicks at y 301 hit the Increment button row (tabs are at y 248-280): ""First"" and ""Second"" each incremented, while ""Third"" and the y 327 increments fell in gaps. End state: forced-on off, forced-off on, switch off, so Set both on and Set opposite (y 537, buttons at y 551-584) and the switch (y 587, switch at y 613-638) missed.","origin=frame: First (127,264), Second (207,264), Third (289,264), Increment (172,304), narrow button (205,383), Wide (209,428), forced-on (134,526), forced-off (226,526), Set both on (149,567), Set opposite (268,567), switch (173,626)"
P13,P13-duplicates-split-width-and-z-order.actions,missed,"Still ""More duplicates (3)"" and ""Narrower (400)"", and Reverse was not pressed. More duplicates spans frame y 137-170, so y 196 hit the ""Identifiable"" text. Reverse spans y 896-929, so y 883 is above it. Separately, the z-order squares are drawn over the ""Top of the stack"" label and the Reverse button (overlap on GTK).","origin=frame: More duplicates (260,153). Narrower (315,432) at the launch layout, re-measure after the duplicate rows are added (about +18pt per row). Reverse (382,912) at the launch layout, same shift"
P14,P14-width-history-and-theme-control.actions,defect,"All the clicks landed: ""Count a rotation (3)"", and the status line was set by the #254 control. Clear history (frame x 16-129, y 348-381) contained the click, but history reads ""0 -> 388 -> 0 -> 388"", not empty. GeometryReader gets a transient width 0 on each relayout, so later clicks append 0 and 388 again. The AppKit capture p14-macos-final-20261015-094236 shows the same 0->388 pairs, so this is framework-level, not GTK-only.",
P15,P15-colour-scheme-and-tall-content.actions,missed,"Reads ""Requested: system"" (expected dark) and no Extra rows. The scheme buttons span frame y 190-223, so the clicks at y 235 fell below them. Use tall content spans y 456-489, so y 446 is above it. The field (""Editable textxy""), toggle (now off) and Button clicks landed.","origin=frame: System (264,207), Light (346,207), Dark (419,207), Use tall content (245,472)"
P15-DARK,P15-DARK-button-under-an-overridden-scheme.actions,missed,"Still ""A button (0)"". The button spans frame y 146-180, so the click at y 209 hit the text field below it. Resolved dark is fine.","origin=frame: A button (280,163)"
P16,P16-split-view-columns.actions,missed,"Force update (3) and three columns are correct, but Science is still selected in all panes. The Humanities click at y 206 hit the bottom of the Science row (y 176-211).","origin=frame: Humanities (62,225)"
P17,P17-picker-aspect-ratio-and-stack-height.actions,missed,"""presses: SML--++"" has no < or >, so Less height and More height never fired (stack 145 x 140). Their clicks at y 736 land in the coloured stack (buttons at frame y 796-829). Separately, the ""picker: 371 x 34"" label is drawn over the picker.","origin=frame: Less height (336,812), More height (469,812)"
P17-DOE,P17-DOE-the-control-clips-too.actions,effect,"The file has no rows. On GTK the capture shows the contrast the DOE needs: the control's orange spills well above and below its blue box, while A cornerRadius(0) and B clipped() are both cut to the box.",
P18,P18-open-and-cancel-each-dialog.actions,missed,"""open -> nothing yet"". Folder and save read cancelled (landed). Open a file spans frame y 204-238, so the click at y 243 is below it.","origin=frame: Open a file (88,221)"
P19,P19-open-the-menu.actions,defect,"The menu click and keys landed (toggle item -> true), but ""last action -> second button item"" instead of ""button item"". On GTK the downArrow count lands one item later than on AppKit: the GTK popover menu opens with an item already focused (or restores the last one). Either GtkBackend's focus-on-open differs from AppKit, or the file needs GTK key counts.",
P20,P20-open-the-nested-menu.actions,defect,"The menu opened (click landed) and downArrow moved past the disabled item to ""Level 2 submenu"", which the capture shows highlighted. The submenu never opened (rightArrow had no effect), and the menu is still open at capture, covering the ""last action"" and ""level 3 toggle"" lines. Keyboard entry into GTK submenus did not happen.",
P21,P21-enabled-and-disabled.actions,missed,"""Button clicks: 1"" (landed, disabled refused), but Toggle false, ToggleSwitch true, Toggle button style false, Checkbox false: none flipped. The rows have no origin (client), and each click is 2-30pt above its control on GTK.","origin=client: Toggle enabled (60,269), Toggle disabled (156,269), ToggleSwitch enabled (103,339), ToggleSwitch disabled (228,339), Toggle button style enabled (60,409), Checkbox enabled (86,475)"
P21,P21-lower-half.actions,missed,"The capture shows the top of the window unscrolled (""Button clicks: 0""), and none of the lower-half fields are visible. The actionfile log has ""-scroll: dx=0 dy=120 ... scrollView=none before=none after=none"", so the scroll did not move the GTK view and every later click landed on top-half blanks.","No coordinate fix: the scroll must first reach the GtkScrolledWindow (or use a taller window), then re-measure the lower-half rows on GTK"
P22,P22-wrapping-width-and-scroll.actions,effect,"Reads ""Wrapping at 350pt"" with the paragraph on two lines (launch is 300). Wider and Narrower are at frame y 493-527, and the clicks landed. The scroll part is not checkable (it ends scrolled back to the top).",
P23,P23-click-a-row.actions,missed,"""selected row: none"". Select row 2 spans frame y 236-270, so the click at y 231 is above it. The row click at (100,558) fell on row 4 (y 540-567), not row 5 (about y 581), and selected nothing. That click is inside a table row, so GTK Table click-to-select is also suspect.","origin=frame: Select row 2 (73,253), row 5 (100,581)"
P23,P23-column-sorting.actions,missed,"""sort: none"", rows unchanged. Sort by Number spans frame y 310-344, so the click at y 292 is above it. The Number header is at about (776,448); the click at (430,413) hit the ""first/last id"" line.","origin=frame: Sort by Number (84,327), Number header (776,448)"
P23,P23-row-selection.actions,missed,"""selected row: none"". Clear selection and Select row 2 at y 231 are above their buttons (y 236-270). The row click at (100,558) landed on row 4 and set no selection (otherwise it would read 3 or 4 after the missed Clear).","origin=frame: row 5 (100,581), Clear selection (200,253), Select row 2 (73,253)"
P23,P23-rows-and-selection.actions,effect,"""rows: 16"" (8 + 4x4 - 2x4, so both More and Fewer landed) and ""Selection on"". The drag text-selection is not visible in the still and is not checkable.",
P24,P24-push-pop-and-outside-state.actions,missed,"""counter -> 2"" and Level 1 are correct, but ""pushes recorded -> 0"" (expected 1). Record a push spans frame y 442-475, so the click at y 440 is just above it.","origin=frame: Record a push (360,459). Re-measure at level 2, where the layout may differ"
P25,P25-drop-zones-at-rest.actions,effect,"The file has no clickable rows. Both zones are the same dark green with blue below green, and both read state idle / received (nothing yet) / type - / count 0. The header reads GtkBackend, as expected for this run.",
P26,P26-swiftcrossui-tab.actions,effect,"The ""[ SwiftCrossUI ]"" tab is selected (launch tab is 0 = Summary in P26.swift), AsyncImage shows the pig, and ""SwiftCrossUI: running"". The click (225,17 client) is far above where the GTK tab bar sits in the final capture (client y about 115-148), so the layout at click time probably differed.",
P27,P27-scroll-the-webview.actions,unclear,"The title and the six gradients have not moved (the negative half holds). But there is no WebView: it shows ""WebKitGTK could not start: libwebkitgtk-6.0.so.4 could not be loaded"", and the scroll log says scrollView=none. ""Delivered and ignored"" cannot be told from ""missed"". GTK on macOS has no working WebView here (a gap).",
P28,P28-hit-testing.actions,effect,"Capture reads ""Clicks received: 2"" with the blue overlay still visible",
P29,P29-disabled-editor.actions,effect,"Editor reads ""Type here if this is not disabledyes"": no ""no"" from the disabled attempt, ""yes"" after Enable; status ""Editor is enabled""",
P30,P30-toggle-the-frame-width.actions,effect,"Button reads ""Use narrow frame"", label ""frame width: 260"", blue rectangle wide",
P31,P31-focus-and-keyboard.actions,defect,"Field reads ""tab"" and the alert opened (log: alert opened), but the ""P31 alert"" with its one OK button is still on screen after Escape. GtkBackend.createAlert installs an Escape shortcut that swallows the key, and present() ignores response -4 (""Ignore escape key for now""), so a one-button alert can't be dismissed with Escape (AppKit gained this on 2026-09-28)",
P32,P32-accessibility-controls.actions,missed,"Partial: ""ab"" typed into the field and ""toggle state: ON"" (both landed). The slider sits at the same spot as in the untouched P32-click-toggle capture, so the drag missed: y334 hits the ""toggle state"" label, and the slider is at y~382. Labelled button (76,206) hit beside the unlabelled square (x 18-52), and the unlabelled toggle (26,238) hit just below it. Unlabelled square unchanged","Labelled button 84,171; unlabelled toggle 35,217; slider mousedown 148,382 move 250,382 mouseup 250,382 (frame)"
P32,P32-click-toggle.actions,missed,"""toggle state: OFF"" and the Toggle label button is unpressed: y289 is in the gap between the text field (bottom ~279) and the Toggle label button (293-325)","Toggle label 72,308 frame"
P33,P33-stepper-and-disclosure.actions,missed,"Reads ""value -1"" (minus landed) and the button reads ""Show details"" (Hide landed), but none of the three plus clicks counted. x120 falls in the gap between the ""value -1"" text and the + button (x 125-166)","plus 145,352 frame (expected end value 2)"
P34,P34-more-rows-and-scrolling.actions,missed,"""requested rows: 500; showing first 500"", so both buttons landed. The list still starts at Row 0 after 20 scroll notches. The pointer (165,425) was inside the list, so the coordinates are not the cause: the log shows ""-scroll ... via HID ... scrollView=none"", and the P57 GTK capture is also unscrolled, so synthesised wheel events don't appear to scroll GtkBackend scroll views","no coordinate fix; to get rows past 0, click ""Scroll to row 50"" at 211,257 frame, or fix wheel delivery to GTK"
P35,P35-state-baseline.actions,effect,"""State baseline: count 4, toggle false""",
P36,P36-picker-button-and-textfield.actions,missed,"Field still reads ""SwiftCrossUI TextField"" with no ""12""; nothing was typed into it. GTK rows are taller: the ""String label button"" click (84,298) landed on the Tagged picker, which now has a focus ring; the picker click (66,240) hit the ""Labelled"" text; the field click (410,331) hit the ""Tagged selection"" text","String label button 93,379; first picker 59,156; text field 410,425 (frame)"
P37,P37-floating-level-and-what-a-replay-cannot-do.actions,defect,"No input involved. Window reads ""supported levels -> automatic, normal"" and ""floating is NOT supported: this window will behave normally"". GtkBackend on macOS offers no .floating level, a feature gap on a shipped backend (the notes expect floating to be supported)",
P38,P38-scroll-the-web-view.actions,defect,"Web frame shows ""WebKitGTK could not start: libwebkitgtk-6.0.so.4 could not be loaded (dlopen ...)"" and ""Navigations reported: 0 (none yet)"". GtkBackend has no working WebView on macOS, so the navigate-and-scroll steps cannot work",
P39,P39-read-nine-cells-against-the-control.actions,effect,"No input involved. All nine effect cells visibly differ from the control: opacity faded, blur soft edges and blurred text, sat0 grey, sat0.5, sat2.5 vivid, brightness, contrast, grayscale, hue-rotated. The AppKit RGB probe values were not re-measured",
P40,P40-read-seven-tiles-and-the-clipping.actions,effect,"No input involved. All seven transforms render (offset, scale 0.6, x1.6/y0.7, rotate centre vs topLeading differ, shear), neighbours did not move. On GTK the tiles spill instead of being clipped, which is what the app text asks for (the AppKit-clipping notes don't apply)",
P41,P41-three-date-picker-styles.actions,defect,"On GTK, .automatic renders as the same calendar grid as .graphical (the style fell back), so the ""stepper up"" clicks at 205,264 selected Aug 12 (.automatic reads 2025-08-12, not 9/24). The .compact click (198,395) landed on the "".compact"" label, not the button (still 2025-08-24). .graphical reads 2025-08-17 (landed). The "".hourMinuteAndSecond"" label also wraps one character per line","compact button 172,431 frame (opens a popover); the .automatic stepper rows cannot apply while .automatic is a calendar on GTK"
P42,P42-scale-factor-starts-at-one.actions,effect,"""current: 2.0"", ""changes observed: 1"", ""1.0 x2 -> 2.0 x4""",
P43,P43-gradient-clipped-to-the-shape.actions,effect,"No input involved. Left circle is a round red-to-blue gradient (corners empty), the flat green control circle is fine, the rectangle gradient fills its corners, and the gradient ring's middle is empty",
P44,P44-clip-the-third-cell.actions,missed,"Label still reads ""third cell: no clipped()"" and cell 3 (""toggled"") still spills with its blue corner. y153 is above the button (button spans y 170-204, x 16-156). Cells 1 and 2 behave as expected (1 spills, 2 is cut)","Clip the third cell 86,187 frame"
P45,P45-press-the-computed-binding-toggle.actions,missed,"The honest toggle landed (""honest: true"", ""setter writes: 1""), but both seed clicks at y482 missed: ""selection: 0, typed: (empty)"", so the sibling-reset check was never set up. The seed buttons are at y 494-527","seeds: selection=2 at 74,510; typed=seeded at 205,510 (frame)"
P45,P45-press-the-contradicting-toggle.actions,defect,"The press landed (log ""stubborn set to true, getter still says false"", setter writes 1), but the GTK toggle button is drawn in its pressed/active state although the binding's getter returns false. GtkBackend doesn't put the native toggle state back to the binding's value. The seed clicks also missed (selection 0, typed empty)","seeds 74,510 and 205,510 (frame)"
P45,P45-press-the-model-button.actions,missed,"The flip honest button landed (""honest: true, setter writes: 1, button presses: 1""), but the seeds missed: ""selection: 0, typed: (empty)"" where 2/""seeded"" was required","seeds 74,510 and 205,510 (frame)"
P45,P45-press-the-right-half.actions,missed,"""selection: 0"": y482 is above the ""selection = 2"" button (y 494-527, x 17-131), so the right-half question was never asked","x0+0.8w = 108,510 frame"
P45,P45-press-the-state-toggle.actions,missed,"stateToggle still reads ✗ and the seeds missed (selection 0, typed empty). y258 is in the gap below the stateToggle button (y 214-247)","stateToggle 77,231; seeds 74,510 and 205,510 (frame)"
P46,P46-increment-the-state-object.actions,missed,"""model.count = 0"", ""observed child sees count = 0"" (constructions 1). y514 is just above the Increment model button (y 517-550, x 12-151)","Increment model 82,534 frame"
P47,P47-draw-every-symbol.actions,defect,"No input involved. The grid has 36 entries and the unknown name draws as text, but about 18 of 36 symbols have no GTK glyph and draw as fallback text truncated to an unreadable ""Pho..."", ""M..."", ""Lo..."", ""Batt..."", ""Setti..."". The unknown name is also cut to ""definitely.not.a.sy..."". P47.swift sets no frame on these, so the fallback text is squeezed into a glyph-sized cell by the backend",
P48,P48-render-the-grids.actions,effect,"No input involved. debug-events/p48-debug-events.log at 18:04:31Z (this run) has ""grids flexible-3 fixed-90.5x2 adaptive-120 hgrid-fixed34x2 hgrid-aligned3"", and the capture shows 1 2 3/4 5 6/7 8, a narrow two-wide block, several per row, 1/2 3/4 5/6 across, and top/center/bottom lanes",
P49,P49-show-the-full-screen-cover.actions,missed,"No cover; counters still read cover opens: 0, coverShown = false. Click (80,329) frame lands in the gap/label ""3. popover..."" below the button (GTK button is at frame y~278).","click 82,278 frame (Show the cover)"
